Hi Andy. One more question...
An option to assess how occupantion changes in time and space, without hurting the population closing premise would be use dynamic explicit models rather than the classical models of single-season. The largest existing parameterization in dynamic models, will result in less parsimonious models probably. Is this correct?
What I lose by choosing dynamic model in detriment of the single-season models?
Regards,
Marina

