As Marc points out the number of detections is quite low.  If you plot something like

    plot(colMeans(Temp),jitter(colMeans(y),factor=0.3))

there doesn't seem to be much to go on to develop a relationship between detection probability and temperature (even if one ignores the uniform confounding with the probability of presence among the 15 sites).

Also, all sites have exactly the same temperature regime.  Are sites not separated so as to have exactly the same temperature or is there only a single nearby weather station?

Jim

On Fri, Mar 14, 2014 at 2:41 PM, Kery Marc <marc...@vogelwarte.ch> wrote:
> Dear all,
>
> of course I am a big fan of BUGS (though you ran JAGS, which is even better perhaps ;)), but, this data set is very problematic in principle: with such extremely small detection probability, the occupancy model is well known to often yield positive biases in occupancy, and often very much so, see the simulations in the original occupancy paper (MacKenzie et al., Ecology, 2002).
