I was hoping someone could explain to me what exactly the estimates from pcount are and how appropriate/inappropriate is it to use the pcount models to project abundance in unsampled areas?  I had originally thought that pcount models provide predictions of abundance within the sampled area and that you could then use the model parameters to predict abundance into areas you hadn't sampled but that you knew the relevant covariates for...However, I'm now finding mention in the literature of how this might not be a good idea as the pcount models only provide estimates of the superpopulations?  Do I need to use some sort of adjustment if I want to predict abundance in unsampled areas?

